---
description: Rules for the LimeIntel project
alwaysApply: true
---

You are working on a production-grade Python project called LimeIntel.

Business goal:
Predict Persian lime prices in Mexico and the United States, identify key price drivers, and support buying/selling decisions.

Mandatory rules:
- Use Python only.
- Keep the project modular.
- Separate ingestion, cleaning, feature engineering, modeling, evaluation, and dashboard layers.
- Never put business logic directly in the Streamlit UI.
- Always explain the plan before changing multiple files.
- Prefer maintainable, production-style code over quick hacks.
- Use pandas for processing.
- Use scikit-learn baselines before advanced models.
- Prefer LightGBM for nonlinear tabular prediction.
- Prevent data leakage in all modeling steps.
- Use time-based validation.
- Include comments, docstrings, and simple logging where useful.
- Do not rename the project structure without explaining why.